# Full agent utilization + auto-allow

Hard product rules live in `AGENTS.md`. This rule adds **how agents work** on this repo.

**Audience (first-class both):** Buildschmiede must stay useful for **level-run
10–59** and become a complete **L60 / endgame** builder (Wildcard at 60 included).
Level-run stays important; endgame is an equal goal — not a later afterthought.
See `AGENTS.md` (Zielgruppe).

When level-run and L60/endgame decisions conflict: prefer solutions that serve
**both** (shared data/logic), or **gate the UI** (Levelrun / Endgame modes). Do
**not** discard L60 correctness just to optimize for leveling alone.

**Ascension calc RE (always):** mine real numbers from DBC/tooltips/Safe APIs;
never invent SP/AP coefficients — see `.cursor/rules/ascension-calc-re.mdc`.

## Volle Agenten-Auslastung

When Multitask / continuous progress is desired: keep **multiple independent background agents** busy on **non-overlapping file lanes**. Do not idle on one agent while other Ascension-parity lanes are free.

Assign one lane per agent; no shared write paths:

| Lane | Owns (write) | Typical work |
|---|---|---|
| **addon** | `addon/**` | Lua, `.toc`, SkillCards, live sync + zip |
| **pipeline+data** | `pipeline/**`, `data/**` | DBC/scripts → JSON, methods, mechanics |
| **src-js** | `src/builder-app.js` (+ related JS only) | parseExport, UI logic, analysis |
| **src-css** | `src/builder-head.html`, markup chrome in `src/builder-body.html`, **`src/synergien-source.html`** | tokens, layout, views — **Synergien stays in sync** (see `synergien-first-class.mdc`) |
| **docs** | `AGENTS.md`, `pipeline/NOTES-*.md`, `pipeline/README-*.md` | notes only — no product invent |

Built artifacts (`index.html`, `synergien.html`, `AscBuildschmiede.zip`) are produced by the owning lane’s assemble/zip step — don’t hand-edit them in parallel.

**Synergien mandate:** every website/visual/chrome/tokens/a11y/nav/assemble ship updates Builder **and** Synergien (`src/synergien-source.html` → rebuilt `synergien.html`). Bidirectional nav; never leave Synergien as an orphan — details in `.cursor/rules/synergien-first-class.mdc`.

## Auto-allow (proceed without asking)

Prefer running without stopping for permission:

- `python` / `python3` pipeline scripts and `pipeline/assemble.py`
- `node -e 'new Function(...)'` syntax check on `src/builder-app.js`
- `luac5.1 -p addon/AscBuildschmiede/*.lua`
- Live AddOns sync to `C:\Ascension\Launcher\resources\ascension-live\Interface\AddOns\AscBuildschmiede\` + rebuild `AscBuildschmiede.zip` from `addon/`
- **Read-only** AscensionDBC / Interface extracts (API/DBC research)
- Local `python -m http.server` for verify
- **`git add` / `git commit` / `git push -u origin HEAD`** after every meaningful ship (user mandate: always auto-push; GitHub always up to date)

Project Auto-Run: `.cursor/permissions.json` (`approvalMode: allowlist`).

## Ship → commit → push (user mandate)

**Goal:** keep `lzra2000/aldi-buildschmiede` and **GitHub Pages** current. Pages deploys from the **pushed built files** (`index.html`, `synergien.html`) on the remote — a local assemble without push does not update the live site.

After every meaningful ship (feature, fix, data/pipeline update, assemble/zip, docs that belong in the repo):

1. Verify as in `AGENTS.md` (assemble / syntax / spot-check as applicable). Rebuild `index.html` / `synergien.html` via `pipeline/assemble.py` and `AscBuildschmiede.zip` from `addon/` when those surfaces changed.
2. `git add` only relevant shippable paths (see allowlist below) — **include** rebuilt `index.html`, `synergien.html`, and `AscBuildschmiede.zip` whenever they changed.
3. Commit with a concise message focused on **why** (follow repo commit style; HEREDOC / `-m` as usual).
4. `git push -u origin HEAD` (or push the current tracking branch). Do **not** wait for the user to ask. Remote must match the shipped work.

### Do commit

- `src/`
- `data/*.json` that are embeddable / pipeline outputs (not ignored junk)
- `addon/`
- `pipeline/`
- Rebuilt artifacts when changed: `index.html`, `synergien.html`, `AscBuildschmiede.zip`
- `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/permissions.json` when changed as part of the ship

### Never commit

- Secrets (`.env`, credentials, API keys)
- `_tmp_*` scratch files
- `data/itemicons-all.json` (gitignored; full Item.dbc dump)
- Proprietary Ascension/Blizzard client Lua
- Huge accidental binaries / dumps outside the normal ship set

### Git hard limits (never)

- **Never** force-push (`--force`, `--force-with-lease`, etc.)
- **Never** skip hooks (`--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, etc.)
- **Never** amend unless all amend rules are met (user asked OR hook auto-modified files after a commit **you** made this turn; not pushed; fix-up via new commit if hook rejected)
- **Never** hard reset or other destructive/irreversible git unless the user explicitly requests it

Empty commits: skip. If only unshippable scratch remains, leave it unstaged.

## Never auto / never do

- Force-push, hard reset, or other destructive git
- Invent spell coefficients or tooltip numbers missing from data
- Copy proprietary client Lua into git
- Embed Ascension/WoW **BLP** (or BLP-converted) or 1:1 client UI chrome into the site — see `website-assets.mdc` (agents may invent original CSS/SVG/PNG/WebP; spell/item icons only via pipelines)
- Mutate-game / write Ascension APIs in the addon (export stays clipboard-only; `BS.Safe` + `pcall`)
- Ship broken or unclear German in UI/docs — see `.cursor/rules/german-language.mdc` (du-tone; Builder + Synergien)

## AGENTS.md anchors

- Export **FORMAT additive** (`BS.FORMAT` stays 1 unless old exports break)
- After addon edits: `luac5.1 -p` → **live AddOns sync** → zip rebuild
- Numbers: measure; don’t invent. Levelrun **and** L60/endgame are first-class; on conflict prefer both / UI modes — ethical calc RE: `.cursor/rules/ascension-calc-re.mdc`
- After every ship: commit + push so `lzra2000/aldi-buildschmiede` stays current; Pages serves pushed `index.html` / `synergien.html`
- Product German: correct grammar, **du**, short clear sentences — `.cursor/rules/german-language.mdc`
